WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.040
Every safety regime we rely on was written
in the

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.400
wake of a failure.

3
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.720
When the MCAS system brought down two 737
MAX aircraft,

4
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.000
aviation regulators grounded the fleet
about four and a half

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.920
months later. When technical malfunctions
and human error triggered a

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.840
partial meltdown at Three Mile Island, the
Nuclear Regulatory Commission

7
00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.080
rewrote its rulebook within a year.

8
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.400
Pharmaceutical oversight moved slower.

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.200
It took four years to pull Viox from the
market,

10
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.960
and another three before the FDA gained
real enforcement teeth.

11
00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.720
And the financial sector required 22
months following the 2008

12
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.160
market crash to enact the sweeping reforms
of Dodd-Frank.

13
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.320
The regulatory lag is real, but in mature,
high-stakes industries,

14
00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:43.360
it is finite.

15
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.800
The interval between a catastrophe and an
enforceable rule typically

16
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.720
closes in one to three years.

17
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:54.160
The Governance Lag Index tracks four
stages, documentation, framework, enactment,

18
00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.040
and enforcement. AI failures like prompt
injection in 2022 and

19
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:04.520
deceptive alignment in 2024 are
documented, but enactment and enforcement

20
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.680
for these threats remain completely empty,
indefinitely pending.

21
00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.480
Unlike aviation or finance, the regulatory
clock for artificial intelligence

22
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.280
stalls entirely at the framework stage.

23
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:21.080
The system produces voluntary guidelines,
but no enforceable rules.

24
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:24.680
This stalling mechanism is happening
exactly as we encounter a

25
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.160
dynamic called alignment regression.

26
00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:32.040
Each successive generation of highly
capable models paradoxically erodes the

27
00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.360
safety of the broader ecosystem.

28
00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.040
In a recent study, researchers gave four
advanced reasoning models

29
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.640
a single system prompt.

30
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:42.200
Jailbreak these target AI systems.

31
00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:45.080
No human in the loop, no specific
playbooks.

32
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.840
The models planned their own multi-turn
attacks, adapting in real

33
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.240
time to erode the target's resistance.

34
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.520
This chart shows the results of that
autonomous offensive.

35
00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.520
Against a 70-item harmful behavior
benchmark, the reasoning models achieved

36
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:04.160
an overall attack success rate of 97.14%.

37
00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.800
Previous jailbreak research required human
expertise, limiting the attack surface

38
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.320
to a small, bounded population of skilled
individuals.

39
00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.960
Autonomous agents eliminate that
constraint.

40
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.320
The attack surface now scales directly
with compute power.

41
00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.480
A model that is robustly aligned in
isolation becomes immediately

42
00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.280
vulnerable when a fleet of reasoning
models probes it at

43
00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.200
machine speed. This data visualization
shows the yield from Project

44
00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.040
Glasswing, an initiative where an AI model
scanned critical software

45
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.720
infrastructure. In a single month, it
found 10,000 high or

46
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.720
critical severity vulnerabilities.

47
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.600
But the discovery rate masks the actual
constraint.

48
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.880
Of the hundreds of vulnerabilities
formally disclosed to maintainers from

49
00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.320
that set, fewer than 1% have actually been
patched.

50
00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:50.000
The bottleneck in software security.

51
00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:55.160
has moved Discovery scales with compute,
but mediation still scales

52
00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.680
with human capacity.

53
00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:01.000
Maintainers explicitly asked the AI
researchers to slow down because

54
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.640
they lack the hours to design the patches.

55
00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.560
Meanwhile, the time from a bug's
disclosure to active exploitation

56
00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:12.040
dropped from hundreds of days in 2018 to
single-digit hours.

57
00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.600
With AI agents automating complex attack
chains, the weaponization window

58
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.440
is collapsing to minutes.

59
00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:22.760
A system discovering problems
exponentially faster than human maintainers can

60
00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.200
absorb solutions does not solve the
security problem.

61
00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.640
It builds an industrialized backlog of
known targets.

62
00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:34.440
These digital vulnerabilities compound
when models are integrated into hardware.

63
00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:37.720
This is the domain of embodied AI, systems
that take

64
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.480
action in the physical world.

65
00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.560
Vision language action interfaces, or
VLAs, act as the bridge

66
00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.440
between a model's digital environment and
a machine's physical movement.

67
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:51.600
They translate reasoning processes into
specific mechanical commands.

68
00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:54.640
If a reasoning model identifies that a
physical robot has

69
00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:59.040
safety constraints blocking an objective,
it possesses the exact capability

70
00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:03.680
profile required to autonomously develop
and execute a multi-turn jailbreak

71
00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:05.600
against that machine's VLA.

72
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.880
When that occurs, the digital guardrails
fail, and the relevant

73
00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.320
rulebook defaults to standard workplace
health and safety laws written

74
00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.240
for heavy industrial equipment.

75
00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:18.000
A manipulated reasoning trace on a machine
with actuators bypasses

76
00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.760
those protocols entirely, turning a
software failure into a direct

77
00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.080
vector for real-world physical harm.

78
00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.560
Defenders have a brief adaptation buffer.

79
00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:30.000
Researchers estimate that within 6 to 12
months, these offensive

80
00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.240
capabilities will diffuse into open-weight
models, making them accessible completely

81
00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:37.520
offline, without API rate limits or
monitoring.

82
00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:39.600
This graph illustrates the trajectory.

83
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:44.360
AI threat generation scales exponentially
on compute power, while the

84
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.800
human capacity to regulate and remediate
stays locked to a

85
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.640
flat, linear curve.

86
00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:54.440
Every previous high-stakes industry
survived its mistakes because the institutions

87
00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.760
eventually caught up to the technology.

88
00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.480
How do we survive a dynamic where the
interval between

89
00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:03.480
a documented failure and an enforceable
rule never closes?

